  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>ATAK's standard plugin UI is the <strong>DropDown</strong> — a panel that slides in over the side of the map. You implement it by extending <code>DropDownReceiver</code>: it is both a <code>BroadcastReceiver</code> (it reacts to the action your tool fires) and the owner of the panel's view.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-receiver-skeleton\"><a href=\"#the-receiver-skeleton\">The receiver skeleton</a></h2>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// Simplified from the example. The real HelloWorldDropDownReceiver also</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// implements SensorEventListener (for a sensor demo) and takes a</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// HelloWorldMapOverlay as a third constructor argument.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> class</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> HelloWorldDropDownReceiver</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> extends</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> DropDownReceiver</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">        implements</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> DropDown</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">OnStateListener</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> static</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> SHOW_HELLO_WORLD </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#98C379\">            \"com.atakmap.android.helloworld.SHOW_HELLO_WORLD\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> View</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> helloView</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    private</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> pluginContext</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> HelloWorldDropDownReceiver</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">MapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> mapView</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">                                      HelloWorldMapOverlay</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75;font-style:italic\"> mapOverlay</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        super</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(mapView);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">        this</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">pluginContext</span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\"> context;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">        // Inflate YOUR layout with the PLUGIN context (resources live in your APK).</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">        helloView </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> PluginLayoutInflater</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">inflate</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">                pluginContext, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">R</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">layout</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">hello_world_layout</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">        // ... wire up the buttons/spinners inside helloView ...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    }</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>The <code>onReceive</code> handler reacts to the action and shows the panel. Note the <strong>re-open guard</strong> and the real <code>showDropDown</code> width/height ratios:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">    public</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> onReceive</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">(</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Context</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> context</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> Intent</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> intent) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">        final</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> String</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> action </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> intent</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getAction</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">        if</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> (action </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">==</span><span style=\"color:#D19A66\"> null</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">            return</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">        switch</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> (action) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">            case</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> SHOW_HELLO_WORLD</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">                if</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">!</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">isClosed</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">()) {          </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// already open? just bring it back</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">                    unhideDropDown</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">()</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">                    return</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">                }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">                //          view,      landscape W/H,        portrait W/H,   ignoreBack, listener</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">                showDropDown</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">(helloView</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> HALF_WIDTH</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> FULL_HEIGHT</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">                        FULL_WIDTH</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> HALF_HEIGHT</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#D19A66\"> false</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> this</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">                break</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">        }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">    @</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Override</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> protected</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> void</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> disposeImpl</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">() { </span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">/* release resources */</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">}</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>Things to notice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>**PluginLayoutInflater.inflate(pluginContext, R.layout.…)**</code> turns your layout XML into a <code>View</code>. Always use the <strong>plugin context</strong> — that's what resolves <code>R.layout</code>, <code>R.drawable</code>, etc. from your APK.</li>\n<li><code>**showDropDown(view, lwFrac, lhFrac, pwFrac, phFrac, ignoreBackButton, listener)**</code> asks ATAK to slide the panel in at the given fractions of the screen — here <code>HALF_WIDTH × FULL_HEIGHT</code> in landscape and <code>FULL_WIDTH × HALF_HEIGHT</code> in portrait (constants provided by the <code>DropDownReceiver</code> base class).</li>\n<li><code>**isClosed()**</code> <strong>/</strong> <code>**unhideDropDown()**</code> let you avoid stacking duplicate panels when the user taps your button again.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-two-context-rule-in-practice\"><a href=\"#the-two-context-rule-in-practice\">The two-Context rule, in practice</a></h2>\n<p>This is the rule from <a href=\"/en/working-with-tak/how-atak-plugins-work-GtuYZlJSnX\">How ATAK plugins work</a>, restated where it actually bites. Inside a receiver you have both contexts available:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Plugin context</strong> (<code>pluginContext</code>) → inflate layouts, load <em>your</em> drawables and strings.</li>\n<li><strong>MapView context</strong> (<code>getMapView().getContext()</code>) → construct <code>AlertDialog</code>s, show <code>Toast</code>s, and anything else that draws on ATAK's screen.</li>\n</ul>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// ✅ correct — dialog/toast use the MapView context</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">new</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> AlertDialog</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">Builder</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getMapView</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">().</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getContext</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">())</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">        .</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setTitle</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"Hello\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">        .</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setMessage</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"From the plugin\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">        .</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">show</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Toast</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">makeText</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getMapView</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">().</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getContext</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(), </span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"Hello\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">, </span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Toast</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">LENGTH_SHORT</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">).</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">show</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">// ❌ wrong — building an AlertDialog with the plugin context throws at runtime</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#C678DD\">new</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> AlertDialog</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">Builder</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(pluginContext)</span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\"> /* ... */</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<p>If a dialog or toast crashes the instant it appears, this is almost always the cause.</p>\n<h2 id=\"putting-something-on-the-map\"><a href=\"#putting-something-on-the-map\">Putting something on the map</a></h2>\n<p>A <code>DropDownReceiver</code> reaches the map through <code>getMapView()</code>. Here is the example's \"drop a marker at screen centre\" handler, lightly trimmed:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "html": "<pre class=\"shiki one-dark-pro\" style=\"background-color:#282c34;color:#abb2bf\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">String</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> uid </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\"> UUID</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">randomUUID</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">().</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">toString</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">GeoPoint</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> location </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> getMapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">()</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getCenterPoint</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">().</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">Marker</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> marker </span><span style=\"color:#56B6C2\">=</span><span style=\"color:#C678DD\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\"> Marker</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">(location</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">,</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\"> uid)</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">marker</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setAlwaysShowText</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#D19A66\">true</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">marker</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setTitle</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"HelloWorld\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">marker</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setType</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#98C379\">\"custom-type\"</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E5C07B\">marker</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">setTouchable</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(</span><span style=\"color:#D19A66\">true</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getMapView</span><span style=\"color:#E06C75\">()</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">.</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">getRootGroup</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">().</span><span style=\"color:#61AFEF\">addItem</span><span style=\"color:#ABB2BF\">(marker);</span><span style=\"color:#7F848E;font-style:italic\">   // now visible on the map</span></span></code></pre>",
      "lang": "java"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "html": "<ul>\n<li><code>getRootGroup()</code> is the top-level <code>MapGroup</code>; adding a <code>MapItem</code> (such as a <code>Marker</code>) to a group is what makes it appear.</li>\n<li><code>setType(...)</code> is the marker's <strong>CoT type</strong>. The example uses a throwaway <code>\"custom-type\"</code>, but real markers use the Cursor-on-Target / MIL-STD-2525 type scheme — e.g. <code>a-f-G-U-C</code> for a friendly ground combat unit, <code>a-u-G</code> for an unknown ground track. Type drives the icon and affiliation colour.</li>\n<li>For richer placement (auto-icons, affiliation, persistence) the example also uses <code>PlacePointTool.MarkerCreator</code>; <code>new Marker(...)</code> is the lowest-level path.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We look at CoT messaging — sending those markers to other ATAK users — next. Prefer Kotlin (or want a Jetpack Compose UI)? See <a href=\"/en/working-with-tak/writing-plugins-in-kotlin-compose-Q4YEtk2N7A\">Writing plugins in Kotlin &#x26; Compose</a>.</p>\n<p>→ Next: <a href=\"/en/working-with-tak/writing-plugins-in-kotlin-compose-Q4YEtk2N7A\">Writing plugins in Kotlin &#x26; Compose</a>, or skip to <a href=\"/en/working-with-tak/working-with-the-map-cot-JmDIw4jN8e\">Working with the map &#x26; CoT</a>.</p>"
    }
  ]
}
